{"kind":"artifact","text":"Draft 5 of the three sales applications note. Since draft 3 (19d0bbfd F1 to F5): supply is four acts with fixed grants, one per domain, guarded by the requirement's domain and the assigned expert as signer; review is one act under bid.review held by the owner and the sales engineer; approvals are per kind (approve-price, approve-terms) and asking an expert is a person's act; intake creates the two required approvals, a later supply resets them, and assemble is refused unless every import row is reviewed or declined, no mapping is proposed, both approvals are granted at the current revisions and a rendering exists at them, with submit naming that exact assembly; publication is pending from the send and confirmed only when the destination's receipt is read back with a matching digest, for the bid and for each post, with unknown held and refusals recorded; retirement replaces the file with a notice and rewrites the index under today's file write; an import holds at most one hundred rows and larger requests are refused at import; several scopes credited to M2a and M2b. Draft 4 added section 2, Why not just an agent.","body":{"commit":"4c082db8b9dde79dcd2c6f97aca7426d92c93052","path":"notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md"}}